the chelsea owner roman abramovich has  become the latest russian oligarch to  have his assets frozen by the uk  government as part of sanctions over the  war in ukraine in a statement outlining  those sanctions the government said  abramovic is associated with a person  who is or has been involved in  destabilizing ukraine and undermining  and threatening the territorial  integrity sovereignty and independence  of ukraine namely vladimir putin with  whom abramovic has a close had excuse me  a close relationship for decades  well joining me now is kaveh sorhikov  from sky sports news um kevin thanks a  lot for joining us a lot of reaction on  social media to to this and the top  question is what does this mean for  chelsea well look effectively chelsea  are in limbo they're only operating uh  because they have a special license from  the government because the governments  say they are a significant cultural  asset so basically what that means is  these sanctions are designed to stop  roman abramovich making any money in the  united kingdom but obviously he owns  chelsea football club and the government  don't want to get involved in a  situation where they shut down  chelsea so they've given the club a  special license and the license is going  to be in place until the 31st of may and  effectively what it means is that they  can carry on playing games fulfilling  their fixtures  but there are a lot of things that they  can't do and there are a lot of things  that they can do so they can play games  their games can be shown on tv they can  continue to receive tv money they can  carry on paying their players they can  carry on paying day-to-day bills  but the things they can't do  they can't sell any more tickets to  their games at home so the only people  who'll be able to go to stamford bridge  to watch them are people who already  have tickets or people who have season  tickets they also will not be able to  sell any merchandise so their club shops  will have to close  and also there are  lots of  details about how much money they're  allowed to spend so for instance at home  games they're allowed to spend up to  five hundred thousand pounds per game  providing uh stewarding security and  also refreshments so you'll still be  able to buy food and drink at stanford  bridge when it comes to away games  they're only allowed to spend up to 20  000 pounds on travel now  i think that's going to be pretty  difficult for premier league club to  stick to because uh these clubs their  players are used to traveling everywhere  how much do they usually spend well i  think you know ballpark figure 30 000  pounds but when they play uh a lot of  times they fly a fly by private jet to  games  they have luxury coaches when it comes  to champions league games in europe they  stay at the best hotels they have their  own  chartered plane to fly them everywhere  so  that i'm struggling to see how they're  going to be able to stick to that but  that is what it says in the license and  when it comes to the future of the club  i mean there's so many question marks  because  uh you know i know some chelsea players  they will be thinking today my god what  is happening how am i going to  be paid in the future am i going to go  did you say this it goes up to may but  the government say that it's being  continually reviewed uh so that is when  it is in place at the moment but that  could change  so as the players are concerned very  uncertain they don't know what's going  to happen to them in the future a lot of  them will be on their phone to their  agents maybe thinking chelsea's not the  right club for me i should be moving  somewhere else roman ravich is  not going to be running the club we're  not going to have as much money as we  used to as far as roman ravish himself  is concerned of course he has been on  the back foot from day one uh  as soon as it became apparent that there  was the threat of sanctions he's been  trying to sort something out with  chelsea what steps in place didn't he  what did he do well the first thing he  did is he came up with a scheme where he  apparently was going to give away  control of the club but retain ownership  and the control was going to be handed  over to the six trustees who run  chelsea's charitable arm the chelsea  foundation any problem with that is that  under uk charity laws that was not  allowed and also the trustees didn't  want to get involved in running a  business as big as chelsea especially a  business that was owned by a russian  oligarch so that plan didn't work a few  days later he released a statement  saying that okay i'm going to sell  chelsea and i'm going to give all the  money away so yeah he said he was going  to give it i mean which was absolutely  incredible because chelsea  most people think chelsea are worth  somewhere between 1.5 and 3 billion  pounds billion billion pounds so for a  businessman to come out and say i'm  going to sell it and give the money away  and he said i'm going to give the money  to a foundation that i'm going to set up  and this foundation is going to benefit  the victims all the victims of the war  in ukraine wasn't clear how he was going  to be able to set up a bank account  because obviously he's a russian  oligarch who's linked to vladimir putin  it wasn't clear how he was going to be  able to get the money how he was going  to be able to sell chelsea when so many  russian banks and businesses are  under sanctions so that plan doesn't  look like it's going to work either  because the government have said that  this license means that he will not be  able to sell chelsea for the time being  so the sale is off but there is a way  around it the government have said that  uh if he wants to sell it as long as he  can prove that the proceeds are not  going to him  the government may be able to issue a  new license which would allow the club  to be sold but he would have to prove  absolutely and satisfy the government  that he wasn't getting the proceeds so  the sale looks to be off it looks uh the  club are in total limbo and effectively  they're really being run by the  government yeah because that was my my  next question who's running chelsea well  they are running the only reason they're  operating is that they have this special  license from the government it's never  been issued before i'm assuming it's i  i've never heard of anything happening  like this what i think the problem the  government had is they didn't want to  take over control of chelsea because if  they seize all roman rambush's assets it  would effectively mean that the  government would be running chelsea and  the taxpayer would be subsidizing  chelsea because chelsea lose a lot of  money last year they lost something like  150 million pounds so if we had the  situation whereby the government was  running chelsea you would have taxpayers  coming out and saying  why are my taxes going towards paying  romelu lukaku 300 000 pounds a week i'm  a taxpayer i don't want my money going  to pay these millionaire footballers you  fly on private jets who are prime pilot  jets around the world so i think what  the government have done is quite clever  is they've managed to sort of take a  step back and distance themselves from  owning and running chelsea but really  the only reason chelsea is continuing to  operate and the only reason they'll be  able to play their game against norwich  tonight is because they have a license  to carry on playing which has been  issued by the government and the  government have made it clear they can  take that license away anytime they want  when he said he was going to sell it was  there any interest in it  there's been lots of interest but the  whole issue has been is from a pr point  of view it was great for roman ramovich  to say  i'm going to sell chelsea and i'm going  to give three billion pounds away to the  victims of this war although he never  made it clear whether it was just going  to be uh the money was going to  ukrainians or russians as well in  ukraine  so i had the feeling that it was a bit  of a pr move as far as he was concerned  i've never heard of any businessman ever  selling something worth three billion  pounds and giving all the proceeds away  as to interest there was a lot of  interest  we know of at least 10 parties who are  interested in buying chelsea 10 but none  of them were willing to pay 3 billion  pounds most of the interest  came from the us historically the kind  of people who are interested in buying  premier league clubs have been from  russia have been from china because they  had the cash right yeah and also it  helps them  um soften their image and project soft  power around the world a lot of interest  from the middle east as well in this  case there's been virtually  no interest obviously from russia  there's no interest from china because  chinese government have clamped down on  foreign investment very little interest  from the middle east there was some  interest in europe  and also a lot of interest from american  sports investors who want to buy premier  league clubs we've already got eight  premier league clubs who are owned all  co-owned  by americans and i think in the future  we're probably looking at chelsea being  owned  by a u.s businessman sports investor but  that could be months and months away  yeah it's going to be interesting  tonight um against norwich you say thank  you cover thanks a lot fascinating thank  you
 

